{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T13:35:56.171951", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Example implementation: locate the nearest obstacle and attempt to break it.\n  # This assumes the environment `env` has an attribute `target_obstacle`\n  # specifying the name of the obstacle to break (e.g., \"stone\", \"water\").\n  state = env._current_state\n  grid = state.grid\n  pos_y, pos_x = state.pos\n\n  obstacle_name = getattr(env, \"target_obstacle\", None)\n  if obstacle_name is None:\n      return []\n\n  # Retrieve the index for the obstacle kind from the world configuration.\n  obstacle_idx = getattr(env.world, f\"{obstacle_name}_index\", None)\n  if obstacle_idx is None:\n      return []\n\n  # Find all cells containing the obstacle.\n  coords = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, obstacle_idx] > 0)\n  if coords.size == 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Choose the closest obstacle (Manhattan distance).\n  distances = np.abs(coords[:, 0] - pos_y) + np.abs(coords[:, 1] - pos_x)\n  target_y, target_x = coords[np.argmin(distances)]\n\n  actions = []\n\n  # Move vertically towards a cell adjacent to the target.\n  while pos_y < target_y - 1:\n      actions.append(0)  # DOWN\n      pos_y += 1\n  while pos_y > target_y + 1:\n      actions.append(1)  # UP\n      pos_y -= 1\n\n  # Move horizontally towards a cell adjacent to the target.\n  while pos_x < target_x - 1:\n      actions.append(2)  # LEFT\n      pos_x += 1\n  while pos_x > target_x + 1:\n      actions.append(3)  # RIGHT\n      pos_x -= 1\n\n  # Finally, use the USE action to attempt breaking the obstacle.\n  actions.append(4)  # USE\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
