{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T13:37:21.058197", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple random policy: keep taking random actions until the task is done\n  # or we exceed the environment's maximum allowed steps.\n  # The environment is assumed to be a CraftLab instance with the following API:\n  #   env.reset() -> observation dict\n  #   env.step(action) -> (reward, done, observation dict)\n  #   env.action_specs() -> dict mapping action names to integer action IDs\n  #   env.max_steps (optional) -> maximum number of steps allowed in the episode\n  # Return the list of actions taken (as integers).\n\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode.\n  _ = env.reset()\n\n  # Determine the set of possible action IDs.\n  action_ids = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  # Determine a step limit: use the environment's max_steps if available,\n  # otherwise fall back to a large default.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  actions_taken = []\n  done = False\n  step = 0\n  # Loop until the task is completed or we hit the step limit.\n  while not done and step < max_steps:\n      # Choose a random action.\n      act = np.random.choice(action_ids)\n      # Perform the action.\n      reward, done, _ = env.step(int(act))\n      # Record the action.\n      actions_taken.append(int(act))\n      step += 1\n\n  return actions_taken", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
