{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T13:44:07.691741", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  obs = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n\n  # Determine a reasonable limit on the number of steps to avoid infinite loops.\n  # Use the max_steps attribute if present, otherwise default to 1000.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Retrieve the mapping from action names to integer indices.\n  action_space = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  # Simple random policy: keep taking random actions until the episode ends\n  # or we exceed the step limit.\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # Sample a random action from the available action indices.\n      action = np.random.choice(action_space)\n\n      # Apply the action to the environment.\n      reward, done, obs = env.step(action)\n\n      # Record the action taken.\n      actions.append(int(action))\n\n      # Stop if the episode has terminated (goal reached or max steps reached).\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  # Return the sequence of actions taken during the episode.\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
