{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T13:52:12.621011", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  env.reset()\n  actions = []\n\n  # Determine a reasonable step limit: use the environment's max_steps if available,\n  # otherwise fall back to a default large number.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Number of possible actions is stored in the world configuration.\n  n_actions = env.world.n_actions\n\n  # Continue taking random actions until the task is completed or the step budget is exhausted.\n  while not env._is_done() and len(actions) < max_steps:\n      # Sample a random action index.\n      action = int(np.random.randint(n_actions))\n      actions.append(action)\n\n      # Apply the action to the environment; the returned tuple is (reward, done, observation).\n      _, _, _ = env.step(action)\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
