{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T14:03:30.006790", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Attempt to acquire and use the appropriate tool to break the given obstacle.\n  The function follows a simple heuristic:\n  1. Map the obstacle name to the required tool name.\n  2. If the tool is already in the agent's inventory, return the USE action.\n  3. Otherwise, retrieve the recipe for the tool and attempt to collect its\n     primitive ingredients (only a stub implementation here).\n  4. If the tool cannot be determined, return an empty action list.\n\n  Args:\n      env: The CraftLab environment instance.\n      obstacle: String identifier of the obstacle (e.g., \"stone\", \"tree\", \"water\").\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A list of action indices that the agent can execute to break the obstacle.\n  \"\"\"\n  # Mapping from obstacle type to the required tool name.\n  obstacle_to_tool = {\n      \"stone\": \"pickaxe\",\n      \"tree\": \"axe\",\n      \"water\": \"boat\",\n  }\n\n  # Resolve the tool name; if unknown, we cannot handle the obstacle.\n  tool_name = obstacle_to_tool.get(obstacle)\n  if tool_name is None:\n      return []\n\n  # Resolve the integer index for the tool using the world's index.\n  tool_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[tool_name]\n\n  # Shortcut: if we already have the tool in inventory, just use the USE action.\n  if env._current_state.inventory[tool_idx] > 0:\n      return [4]  # 4 corresponds to the USE action.\n\n  # Retrieve the primitive requirements for crafting the tool.\n  # This returns a dict {primitive_idx: count}.\n  primitives_needed = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(tool_idx)\n\n  # If there is no recipe (empty dict), we cannot craft the tool.\n  if not primitives_needed:\n      return []\n\n  # Simple heuristic: try to collect each required primitive by moving towards the\n  # nearest cell that contains it and performing a USE action.\n  # The full path\u2011finding and action sequencing is beyond the scope of this\n  # placeholder implementation, so we return an empty list to indicate that\n  # further planning is required.\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T14:03:31.136731", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
