{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T14:23:54.055461", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and get the initial observation.\n  obs = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n\n  # Determine a reasonable maximum number of steps to attempt.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Main loop: take random actions until the task is done or we exceed max_steps.\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # If the environment reports completion, exit early.\n      if hasattr(env, \"_is_done\") and env._is_done():\n          break\n\n      # Sample a random valid action.\n      # action_specs() returns a dict mapping action names to indices.\n      action_space = env.action_specs()\n      action = np.random.randint(0, len(action_space))\n\n      # Execute the action and collect the result.\n      reward, done, obs = env.step(action)\n\n      # Record the action taken.\n      actions.append(action)\n\n      # If the environment signals termination, stop.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  # Return the sequence of actions taken during the episode.\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
