{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T14:31:46.306369", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple random policy to interact with the environment until the task is completed\n  # or the maximum number of steps is reached.\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  obs = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n  done = False\n\n  # Retrieve the list of possible action indices from the environment.\n  possible_actions = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  # Loop until the environment signals that the episode is done.\n  while not done:\n      # Choose an action uniformly at random.\n      act = np.random.choice(possible_actions)\n\n      # Execute the action in the environment.\n      reward, done, obs = env.step(act)\n\n      # Record the action taken.\n      actions.append(act)\n\n      # Safety check to avoid infinite loops in case the environment never signals done.\n      if len(actions) >= getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000) * 2:\n          break\n\n  # Return the sequence of actions performed.\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T14:31:47.424148", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Return a list of action indices that can be used to break the specified obstacle.\n  The function makes a minimal effort: it maps known obstacles to the generic\n  ``USE`` action (index 4) and returns that action. If the obstacle is unknown,\n  an empty list is returned.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      The CraftLab / CraftWorld environment instance.  It is not used directly\n      in this simple implementation but is kept in the signature for\n      compatibility with more elaborate strategies.\n  obstacle : str\n      Name of the obstacle to break (e.g., ``\"tree\"``, ``\"stone\"``, ``\"water\"``).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A list containing the action index(es) required to break the obstacle.\n      Currently this is just ``[4]`` (the ``USE`` action) for known obstacles.\n  \"\"\"\n  # Mapping from obstacle names to the generic ``USE`` action.\n  # The mapping exists mainly for readability; all known obstacles share the\n  # same action in the current implementation.\n  known_obstacles = {\"tree\", \"stone\", \"water\", \"bush\", \"rock\"}\n\n  # If the obstacle is recognised, return the ``USE`` action (index 4).\n  # Otherwise return an empty list indicating that no breaking action is\n  # defined for the given obstacle.\n  return [4] if obstacle in known_obstacles else []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
