{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T14:44:23.275338", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  obs = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n\n  # Determine a reasonable limit for steps. Use the environment's max_steps if available,\n  # otherwise fall back to a default large number.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Retrieve the mapping from action names to integer indices.\n  action_space = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  # Perform a simple random policy: at each step, select a random action from the\n  # available action space, execute it, and record the action. Stop when the episode\n  # ends (goal achieved or max steps reached).\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      act = np.random.choice(action_space)\n      reward, done, obs = env.step(act)\n      actions.append(int(act))\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
