{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T14:50:17.320030", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Determine the action index corresponding to the \"USE\" action.\n  # Most environments expose an `action_specs` method that maps action names to indices.\n  use_action = 4  # Default index for USE if we cannot infer it.\n  try:\n      # env may be a CraftLab or similar wrapper with action_specs.\n      specs = env.action_specs()\n      # Find the key that matches \"USE\" (case-insensitive).\n      for name, idx in specs.items():\n          if name.strip().upper() == \"USE\":\n              use_action = idx\n              break\n  except Exception:\n      # If any error occurs (e.g., env has no action_specs), keep the default.\n      pass\n\n  # Return a simple plan: use the tool (or attempt to break) at the current location.\n  # More sophisticated logic (moving toward the obstacle, crafting required tools, etc.)\n  # can be built on top of this scaffold.\n  return [use_action]", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
