{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:00:03.599211", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Access the current state from the environment\n  state = env._current_state\n  grid = state.grid\n  pos = state.pos          # (x, y)\n  direction = state.dir   # integer 0\u20113 corresponding to DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT\n\n  # Mapping from direction index to a displacement vector\n  # (matches the order used in CraftLab.action_specs)\n  delta = [(0, 1),   # DOWN\n           (0, -1),  # UP\n           (-1, 0),  # LEFT\n           (1, 0)]   # RIGHT\n\n  # If direction is out of the expected range, we cannot compute a target cell\n  if direction < 0 or direction >= len(delta):\n      return []\n\n  dx, dy = delta[direction]\n  tx, ty = pos[0] + dx, pos[1] + dy\n\n  # Verify the target cell lies inside the grid bounds\n  if not (0 <= tx < grid.shape[0] and 0 <= ty < grid.shape[1]):\n      return []\n\n  # Examine the contents of the cell directly in front of the agent\n  cell_contents = grid[tx, ty, :]\n  if not cell_contents.any():\n      # Empty cell \u2013 nothing to break\n      return []\n\n  # Identify the kind (index) present in the cell (the first non\u2011zero entry)\n  kind = int(np.argmax(cell_contents))\n\n  # If the kind is part of the non\u2011grabbable set, it is an obstacle that can be\n  # acted upon with the USE action (assuming the appropriate tool is already\n  # in the inventory).  The environment will handle whether the tool is\n  # sufficient.\n  if kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      use_action = env.action_specs()['USE']\n      return [use_action]\n\n  # Otherwise the cell contains a grabbable item; no breaking needed.\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
