{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:04:36.564942", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Retrieve the goal index from the environment's task\n  goal_idx = getattr(env, \"task\", None)\n  if goal_idx is None:\n      # If task attribute not present, cannot determine goal; return empty actions\n      return []\n\n  goal_idx = goal_idx.goal if isinstance(goal_idx, tuple) else getattr(env.task, \"goal\", None)\n  if goal_idx is None:\n      return []\n\n  # Get the list of possible action indices\n  action_dict = env.action_specs()\n  possible_actions = list(action_dict.values())\n\n  actions = []\n  max_steps = 200  # safety limit to avoid infinite loops\n\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # Check if the current state already satisfies the goal\n      if env._current_state.satisfies(\"\", goal_idx):\n          break\n\n      # Sample a random action (including movement and USE)\n      act = np.random.choice(possible_actions)\n      actions.append(int(act))\n\n      # Perform the action in the environment\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n      # If the environment reports done (e.g., max steps reached), stop early\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
