{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:05:32.088908", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple random policy: keep taking random actions until the task is done\n  # or a reasonable step limit is reached.  The function returns the\n  # sequence of action indices taken.\n  # Reset the environment to start a fresh episode.\n  _ = env.reset()\n\n  # Gather the possible action indices from the environment spec.\n  action_spec = env.action_specs()\n  possible_actions = list(action_spec.values())\n\n  # Determine a step limit \u2013 use the environment's max_steps if present,\n  # otherwise fall back to a default.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  actions_taken = []\n  done = False\n  steps = 0\n\n  while not done and steps < max_steps:\n      # Choose a random action from the allowed set.\n      a = int(np.random.choice(possible_actions))\n      actions_taken.append(a)\n\n      # Execute the action; the step method returns (reward, done, obs).\n      _, done, _ = env.step(a)\n      steps += 1\n\n  return actions_taken", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
