{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:07:15.564807", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to a clean start (seed for reproducibility)\n  env.reset(seed=0)\n\n  # Prepare a list to collect the actions we will execute\n  actions = []\n\n  # Determine a reasonable horizon \u2013 use the environment's max_steps if\n  # it exists, otherwise fall back to a default.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 200)\n\n  # Obtain the mapping from action names to integer codes.\n  # The values are the actual integer actions the environment expects.\n  action_codes = list(env.action_specs().values())\n  n_actions = len(action_codes)\n\n  # Simple deterministic policy:\n  #   - Cycle through the available actions (e.g., move in each direction,\n  #     then USE) repeatedly.\n  #   - Stop early if the task is already completed.\n  for step in range(max_steps):\n      # If the environment reports that the episode is done (goal reached or\n      # step limit exceeded), exit the loop.\n      if hasattr(env, \"_is_done\") and env._is_done():\n          break\n\n      # Choose the next action in a round\u2011robin fashion.\n      act = action_codes[step % n_actions]\n\n      # Execute the action; CraftLab.step returns (reward, done, observation).\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n      # Record the action we just took.\n      actions.append(act)\n\n      # If the environment signals termination, stop issuing actions.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  # Return the complete list of actions that were taken.\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
