{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:07:56.516595", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple random policy: keep taking random actions until the episode ends or a step limit is reached.\n  actions = []\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  _ = env.reset()\n  done = False\n  steps = 0\n  # Use a reasonable upper bound to avoid infinite loops if something goes wrong.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n  # Extract the list of possible action indices from the environment's action specifications.\n  possible_actions = list(env.action_specs().values())\n  # Main loop: sample random actions until the episode signals done or we hit the step limit.\n  while not done and steps < max_steps:\n      # Choose a random action index.\n      action = int(np.random.choice(possible_actions))\n      actions.append(action)\n      # Execute the action in the environment.\n      _, done, _ = env.step(action)\n      steps += 1\n  # Return the sequence of actions taken.\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
