{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:10:26.314669", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Initialize the environment (reset to start a new episode)\n  try:\n      env.reset()\n  except Exception:\n      # If reset is not available, ignore and proceed\n      pass\n\n  actions = []\n  max_steps = 1000  # safety limit to avoid infinite loops\n\n  # Try to step through the environment using a simple exhaustive action sequence\n  done = False\n  step_count = 0\n  while not done and step_count < max_steps:\n      # Cycle through the basic actions: DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT, USE (assumed indices 0-4)\n      for a in range(5):\n          try:\n              reward, done, obs = env.step(a)\n          except Exception:\n              # If env.step returns a different signature, try to handle gracefully\n              try:\n                  result = env.step(a)\n                  if isinstance(result, tuple) and len(result) == 3:\n                      reward, done, obs = result\n                  else:\n                      # Fallback: assume done flag is second element\n                      reward, done = result[0], result[1]\n                      obs = result[2] if len(result) > 2 else None\n              except Exception:\n                  # If stepping fails, break out\n                  done = True\n                  break\n          actions.append(a)\n          step_count += 1\n          if done or step_count >= max_steps:\n              break\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
