{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:16:09.164536", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Map known obstacles to the tool required to clear them.\n  tool_map = {\"tree\": \"axe\", \"stone\": \"pickaxe\", \"water\": \"boat\"}\n  tool_name = tool_map.get(obstacle)\n  if tool_name is None:\n      return []\n\n  # Resolve the integer ids for the tool and for the USE action.\n  tool_idx = env.world.cookbook.index(tool_name)\n  USE = 4  # constant from CraftLab.action_specs\n\n  # If the tool is already in the agent's inventory, a single USE action\n  # will break the obstacle (the environment logic will handle the actual\n  # removal of the block).\n  if env._current_state.inventory[tool_idx] > 0:\n      return [USE]\n\n  # Otherwise try to craft the tool using the recipe information.\n  # ``primitives_for`` returns a dict mapping primitive indices to the\n  # required counts for a single unit of the goal item.\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(tool_idx)\n  if not recipe:\n      # No known recipe \u2013 we cannot obtain the tool.\n      return []\n\n  # Simple heuristic: if all required primitives are already in the\n  # inventory, we can issue a USE action after crafting.  Crafting in the\n  # real environment requires the agent to move to the appropriate\n  # workshop, which is beyond the scope of this helper.  We therefore\n  # return an empty list to indicate that higher\u2011level planning is needed.\n  have_all = all(env._current_state.inventory[p] >= c for p, c in recipe.items())\n  if have_all:\n      # Assume the tool will be crafted externally; once it exists we can\n      # use it to break the obstacle.\n      return [USE]\n\n  # If we do not have the needed primitives, we cannot break the obstacle\n  # at the moment.\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
