{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:17:26.477542", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple baseline: take random actions until the episode terminates\n  # or a hard step limit is reached.  The function returns the\n  # sequence of action indices taken.\n  actions = []\n\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode\n  env.reset()\n\n  # Determine the available action identifiers from the environment\n  try:\n      action_ids = list(env.action_specs().values())\n  except Exception:\n      # Fallback: if the environment does not expose action_specs,\n      # assume a contiguous range based on n_actions attribute.\n      if hasattr(env, \"n_actions\"):\n          action_ids = list(range(env.n_actions))\n      else:\n          raise RuntimeError(\"Unable to infer action space from the environment.\")\n\n  # Hard limit to avoid infinite loops in pathological cases\n  MAX_STEPS = 2000\n\n  for _ in range(MAX_STEPS):\n      # Choose a random action from the available set\n      act = np.random.choice(action_ids)\n\n      # Execute the action; step returns (reward, done, observation)\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n      # Record the action taken\n      actions.append(int(act))\n\n      # Stop if the episode reports completion\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
