{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:19:49.536446", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Initialize a list to store the actions taken.\n  actions = []\n\n  # Reset the environment if a reset method is available.\n  # Some environments may already be reset by the caller, so we guard with hasattr.\n  if hasattr(env, \"reset\"):\n      _ = env.reset()\n\n  # Retrieve the mapping of action names to integer indices.\n  # The values of this dictionary are the valid action indices.\n  action_spec = env.action_specs()\n  possible_actions = list(action_spec.values())\n\n  # Determine the maximum number of steps we are allowed to take.\n  # If the environment exposes a `max_steps` attribute use it,\n  # otherwise fall back to a generous default.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Main interaction loop: keep stepping until the task is done\n  # or we exceed the step budget.\n  done = False\n  steps = 0\n  while not done and steps < max_steps:\n      # Choose an action uniformly at random from the available set.\n      # This simple policy is sufficient as a generic fallback.\n      action = int(np.random.choice(possible_actions))\n\n      # Apply the action; the step method returns (reward, done, observation).\n      # We only need the `done` flag to decide when to stop.\n      _, done, _ = env.step(action)\n\n      # Record the action for later inspection or playback.\n      actions.append(action)\n\n      steps += 1\n\n  # Return the full sequence of action indices that were executed.\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
