{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:29:20.779819", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  # Reset the environment and obtain the initial observation\n  # (ignore the seed argument; using default reset behavior)\n  obs = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n\n  # Determine a reasonable step limit.  If the environment provides a\n  # task with a step budget, use it; otherwise fall back to a large\n  # default.\n  try:\n      max_steps = int(env.task.steps)\n  except Exception:\n      max_steps = 1000\n\n  done = False\n  steps = 0\n\n  # Simple random\u2011action baseline: keep taking random actions until the\n  # episode terminates or we exceed the step budget.\n  while not done and steps < max_steps:\n      # Randomly choose one of the five possible actions:\n      #   0 = DOWN, 1 = UP, 2 = LEFT, 3 = RIGHT, 4 = USE\n      action = int(np.random.choice([0, 1, 2, 3, 4]))\n      reward, done, obs = env.step(action)\n      actions.append(action)\n      steps += 1\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": -1}}
