{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:30:23.133569", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple random\u2011policy planner that keeps interacting with the environment\n  # until the task is completed (or a step limit is reached).  It prefers\n  # using the `USE` action when a grabbable object is in the immediate 3\u00d73\n  # neighbourhood; otherwise it moves randomly.\n  #\n  # The function returns the list of action indices taken during the episode.\n  #\n  # Assumptions about the `env` object (CraftLab):\n  #   - `env.reset()` initializes the episode and returns the initial observation.\n  #   - `env.step(action)` executes `action` and returns (reward, done, observation).\n  #   - `env._is_done()` tells whether the goal has been satisfied or the max steps\n  #     limit has been reached.\n  #   - `env.world` gives access to the underlying `CraftWorld` instance, which\n  #     contains `n_actions` and `grabbable_indices`.\n  #   - `env._current_state` holds the active `CraftState` instance, which provides\n  #     the `next_to(kind_idx)` method to test adjacency.\n  #   - The action mapping can be obtained via `env.action_specs()`; the `USE`\n  #     action is typically index 4 but we retrieve it safely.\n  #\n  # This implementation is deliberately simple; it is sufficient for many\n  # environments where random exploration eventually discovers the required\n  # primitives and crafts the goal.\n  max_steps = 1000  # safety cap to avoid infinite loops\n  actions_taken = []\n\n  # Reset the environment to start a fresh episode.\n  _ = env.reset()\n\n  # Resolve the integer index for the `USE` action (fallback to 4).\n  use_action = env.action_specs().get(\"USE\", 4)\n\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # Stop if the environment reports completion.\n      if env._is_done():\n          break\n\n      # Access the current state for adjacency checks.\n      state = env._current_state\n\n      # Prefer to `USE` when a grabbable entity is nearby.\n      chosen_action = None\n      for kind_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n          if state.next_to(kind_idx):\n              chosen_action = use_action\n              break\n\n      # If no immediate target, pick a random movement action.\n      if chosen_action is None:\n          # Randomly select among all actions; if the random choice happens\n          # to be `USE` it will simply have no effect when nothing is adjacent.\n          chosen_action = np.random.randint(0, env.world.n_actions)\n\n      # Execute the action.\n      reward, done, _ = env.step(chosen_action)\n\n      # Record the action.\n      actions_taken.append(int(chosen_action))\n\n      # If the environment signals termination, exit early.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions_taken", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
