{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:40:09.746178", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Return a zero-filled vector matching the environment's feature dimension.\n  # If the environment is None or its size cannot be determined, return an empty array.\n  if env is None:\n      return np.array([], dtype=np.float32)\n\n  size = None\n  # Try to infer the feature vector length from common attributes.\n  if hasattr(env, \"world\"):\n      if hasattr(env.world, \"n_features\"):\n          size = env.world.n_features\n      elif hasattr(env.world, \"n_kinds\"):\n          size = env.world.n_kinds\n  if size is None:\n      size = getattr(env, \"n_features\", None)\n\n  if size is None:\n      return np.array([], dtype=np.float32)\n\n  return np.zeros(size, dtype=np.float32)", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:40:10.844970", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Return a zero\u2011vector matching the feature dimension of the environment.\n  if env is None:\n      return np.array([], dtype=np.float32)\n\n  # Try to infer the size from the world object first.\n  size = None\n  if hasattr(env, \"world\"):\n      if hasattr(env.world, \"n_features\"):\n          size = env.world.n_features\n      elif hasattr(env.world, \"n_kinds\"):\n          size = env.world.n_kinds\n\n  # Fallback to attributes directly on the env.\n  if size is None:\n      size = getattr(env, \"n_features\", None) or getattr(env, \"n_kinds\", None)\n\n  # If we still cannot determine a size, return an empty array.\n  if size is None:\n      return np.array([], dtype=np.float32)\n\n  # Return a zero vector of the appropriate length.\n  return np.zeros(size, dtype=np.float32)", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": -1}}
