{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:44:39.190154", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  # Reset the environment to obtain the initial observation.\n  # The reset method returns a dictionary of observations.\n  obs = env.reset()\n\n  # Prepare a list to record the sequence of actions taken.\n  actions_taken = []\n\n  # Determine a reasonable step limit to avoid infinite loops.\n  # Prefer the max_steps attribute if present; otherwise fall back to a default.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 200)\n\n  done = False\n  steps = 0\n\n  # Main interaction loop: keep acting until the episode ends or the step budget is exhausted.\n  while not done and steps < max_steps:\n      # Sample a random valid action.  The action space can be obtained from the\n      # environment's action specifications, which map action names to integer ids.\n      action_spec = env.action_specs()\n      # The spec is a dict; its length gives the number of distinct actions.\n      random_action = int(np.random.randint(len(action_spec)))\n\n      # Execute the chosen action.\n      reward, done, _ = env.step(random_action)\n\n      # Record the action.\n      actions_taken.append(random_action)\n\n      steps += 1\n\n  # Return the list of actions performed during this episode.\n  return actions_taken", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
