{"timestamp": "2025-11-05T15:49:46.578492", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Mapping from obstacle type to the required tool name.\n  obstacle_tool = {\n      \"stone\": \"pickaxe\",\n      \"water\": \"boat\",\n      \"tree\":  \"axe\",\n  }\n\n  # Normalise the obstacle string and look up the needed tool.\n  tool_name = obstacle_tool.get(str(obstacle).lower())\n  if tool_name is None:\n      # Unknown obstacle \u2013 nothing we can do.\n      return []\n\n  # Resolve the integer indices for the tool and the USE action.\n  # The world holds an Index that maps names to ids.\n  tool_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[tool_name]\n\n  # The USE action is the last action in the action space (see\n  # CraftLab.action_specs which maps USE \u2192 4).  We retrieve it from the\n  # environment to stay robust to possible future changes.\n  use_action = None\n  for name, idx in env.action_specs().items():\n      if name.upper() == \"USE\":\n          use_action = idx\n          break\n  if use_action is None:\n      # Fallback to the known constant if the spec is missing.\n      use_action = 4\n\n  # If the required tool is already in the inventory, we can simply\n  # issue a USE action on the obstacle.\n  if hasattr(env, \"_current_state\") and \\\n     env._current_state.inventory[tool_idx] > 0:\n      return [use_action]\n\n  # Otherwise we need to craft the tool.  Crafting in the full\n  # environment would require navigation to a workshop and gathering\n  # primitives, which is beyond the scope of this simple helper.\n  # For now we return a single USE action; the higher\u2011level policy can\n  # decide how to obtain the tool before calling this function again.\n  return [use_action]", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
